@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `br-interpretation-time`

-- Tests for br-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Every expected value below was worked out by hand from the text before the file was run:
-- art. 1 caput (N days after = the Nth day after, the start not counted), art. 1 par. 1 and art. 7 par. 6
-- (N calendar months or years on, the same day number, refused where that month has no such day),
-- art. 19 sole paragraph (counted from: refused at the two boundaries). The calendar facts are those of the Gregorian calendar:
-- 2024 is a leap year, 2025 and 2026 are not; 14 and 15 March 2026 are a Saturday and a Sunday.

§ `Art. 1 caput: N days after a day`

-- the forty-five days of art. 1
#ASSERT `the term in days before a law binds throughout Brazil` EQUALS 45
#ASSERT `the term in months before Brazilian law binds in a foreign State that admits it` EQUALS 3

#ASSERT `the day` 45 `days after` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 24
#ASSERT `the day` 45 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 15
#ASSERT `the day` 45 `days after` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 14
#ASSERT `the day` 45 `days after` (YMD 2024 1 16) EQUALS YMD 2024 3 1
#ASSERT `the day` 45 `days after` (YMD 2023 1 16) EQUALS YMD 2023 3 2

-- a period of one day, and of none
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `days after` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 11
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `days after` (YMD 2026 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `days after` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `days after` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2024 3 1
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `days after` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `the day` 0 `days after` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the day` 30 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31

-- a count that is not a whole number, or is negative, is not a period
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1.5 `days after` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "a period counted after a day is a whole number of units, none of them negative"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "a period counted after a day is a whole number of units, none of them negative"

§ `Art. 1 par. 1: N months after a day`

#ASSERT `the day` 3 `months after` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 10
#ASSERT `the day` 3 `months after` (YMD 2025 11 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 15
#ASSERT `the day` 12 `months after` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2026 7 16
#ASSERT `the day` 0 `months after` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10

-- one month: the month reached must have the day's number
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 15
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 12 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 15
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 28) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2024 1 29) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 3 30) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 30
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `the day` 2 `months after` (YMD 2025 10 31) EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31

-- a start on the 31st, and on the 29th, 30th and 31st into February, and a month of 30 days
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 31) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 30) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 29) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2024 1 30) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2024 1 31) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 3 31) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 3 `months after` (YMD 2025 11 30) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 2 `months after` (YMD 2025 12 31) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1.5 `months after` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "a period counted after a day is a whole number of units, none of them negative"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (0 MINUS 1) `months after` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "a period counted after a day is a whole number of units, none of them negative"

§ `Art. 7 par. 6: N years after a day`

-- the worked cases of the brief
#ASSERT `the day` 3 `years after` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `the day` 5 `years after` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
#ASSERT `the day` 5 `years after` (YMD 2025 9 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 9 1
#ASSERT `the day` 2 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"

-- one year, and the leap day
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `years after` (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `years after` (YMD 2023 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 28
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `years after` (YMD 2023 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2024 12 31
#ASSERT `the day` 4 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29
#ASSERT `the day` 0 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 2 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 3 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1 `years after` (YMD 2028 2 29) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` 1.5 `years after` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "a period counted after a day is a whole number of units, none of them negative"

§ `Art. 19 sole paragraph: the last day of a period counted from a day`

-- the text does not say whether the starting day counts, for any unit
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 30 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 1 15) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `months counted from` (YMD 2025 1 31) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 3 `years counted from` (YMD 2025 7 16) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 5 `years counted from` (YMD 2025 1 15) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 5 `years counted from` (YMD 2025 9 1) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 2 `years counted from` (YMD 2024 2 28) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `years counted from` (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"

-- weeks are never used by the text
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the text never speaks of weeks, so no provision counts a period of weeks"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 2 `weeks counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the text never speaks of weeks, so no provision counts a period of weeks"

-- the two readings, each under its own name; their answers differ by exactly one day
#ASSERT `the last day of N days counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 30 (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `the last day of N days counted from, if the starting day is the first day` 30 (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 30
#ASSERT `the last day of N days counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 1 (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2
#ASSERT `the last day of N days counted from, if the starting day is the first day` 1 (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `the last day of N days counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 90 (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 8
#ASSERT `the last day of N days counted from, if the starting day is the first day` 90 (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 7
#ASSERT `the last day of N months counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 1 (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 15
#ASSERT `the last day of N months counted from, if the starting day is the first day` 1 (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 14
#ASSERT `the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 3 (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is the first day` 3 (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 15
#ASSERT `the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 5 (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
#ASSERT `the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is the first day` 5 (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 14
#ASSERT `the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 5 (YMD 2025 9 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 9 1
#ASSERT `the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is the first day` 5 (YMD 2025 9 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 8 31
#ASSERT `the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 2 (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is the first day` 2 (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 27
-- where the month reached lacks the day, neither reading has an answer
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of N months counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 1 (YMD 2025 1 31) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of N months counted from, if the starting day is the first day` 1 (YMD 2025 1 31) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 1 (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of N years counted from, if the starting day is the first day` 1 (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"

§ `Art. 19 sole paragraph: whether a day falls inside a period of days counted from a start`

-- ten days from 1 January 2026: the 2nd to the 10th are inside on both readings, the 1st and the 11th on one only
#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 2) `falls inside a period of` 10 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 5) `falls inside a period of` 10 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 10) `falls inside a period of` 10 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `falls inside a period of` 10 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 11) `falls inside a period of` 10 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `falls inside a period of` 10 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 12) `falls inside a period of` 10 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1)

-- one day from 1 January 2026: no day is inside on both readings
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `falls inside a period of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 2) `falls inside a period of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `falls inside a period of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 3) `falls inside a period of` 1 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1)

-- two days from 1 January 2026: only the 2nd is inside on both
#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 2) `falls inside a period of` 2 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `falls inside a period of` 2 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 3) `falls inside a period of` 2 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 4) `falls inside a period of` 2 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1)

-- ninety days from 10 March 2026, across the end of three months: the 90th day is 8 June
#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2026 3 11) `falls inside a period of` 90 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2026 4 30) `falls inside a period of` 90 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2026 6 7) `falls inside a period of` 90 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 3 10) `falls inside a period of` 90 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 6 8) `falls inside a period of` 90 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2026 3 9) `falls inside a period of` 90 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2026 6 9) `falls inside a period of` 90 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 3 10)

-- a period over a leap day: three days from 28 February 2024 are 29 February, 1 and 2 March
#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2024 2 29) `falls inside a period of` 3 `days counted from` (YMD 2024 2 28)
#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2024 3 1) `falls inside a period of` 3 `days counted from` (YMD 2024 2 28)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2024 2 28) `falls inside a period of` 3 `days counted from` (YMD 2024 2 28) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2024 3 2) `falls inside a period of` 3 `days counted from` (YMD 2024 2 28) BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2024 3 3) `falls inside a period of` 3 `days counted from` (YMD 2024 2 28)

-- a period that is not a whole number of days, at least one
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 5) `falls inside a period of` 0 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "a period counted from a day is a whole number of days, at least one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 5) `falls inside a period of` 2.5 `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "a period counted from a day is a whole number of days, at least one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 5) `falls inside a period of` (0 MINUS 3) `days counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "a period counted from a day is a whole number of days, at least one"

§ `Days of rest, holidays and recess: the input is read and the text has no rule`

-- 14 and 15 March 2026 are a Saturday and a Sunday
`a weekend` MEANS LIST (YMD 2026 3 14), (YMD 2026 3 15)
`a weekend with the Friday a holiday` MEANS LIST (YMD 2026 3 13), (YMD 2026 3 14), (YMD 2026 3 15)
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`no day of rest` MEANS EMPTY

#ASSERT `Weekday of` (YMD 2026 3 14) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `Weekday of` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS 0

-- a last day that is not a day of rest is its own last day, whatever else is in the list
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `a weekend` (YMD 2026 3 13) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 13
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `a weekend` (YMD 2026 3 16) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 16
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `no day of rest` (YMD 2026 3 14) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `a weekend with the Friday a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 16) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 16

-- a last day that is a day of rest is refused: one day of rest, and two in a row, and three in a row
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `a weekend` (YMD 2026 3 14) BECAUSE "the text has no rule that moves the last day of a period off a day of rest, a holiday or a recess"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `a weekend` (YMD 2026 3 15) BECAUSE "the text has no rule that moves the last day of a period off a day of rest, a holiday or a recess"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `a weekend with the Friday a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 13) BECAUSE "the text has no rule that moves the last day of a period off a day of rest, a holiday or a recess"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `a weekend with the Friday a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 14) BECAUSE "the text has no rule that moves the last day of a period off a day of rest, a holiday or a recess"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `a weekend with the Friday a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 15) BECAUSE "the text has no rule that moves the last day of a period off a day of rest, a holiday or a recess"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` (LIST (YMD 2026 3 11)) (YMD 2026 3 11) BECAUSE "the text has no rule that moves the last day of a period off a day of rest, a holiday or a recess"

-- composed: five days after 9 March 2026 is Saturday 14 March; four days after it is Friday 13 March
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `a weekend` (`the last day of N days counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 5 (YMD 2026 3 9)) BECAUSE "the text has no rule that moves the last day of a period off a day of rest, a holiday or a recess"
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `a weekend` (`the last day of N days counted from, if the starting day is not counted` 4 (YMD 2026 3 9)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 13
-- a holiday in the middle of the week is a day of rest too, because the input says so and not because of a calendar here
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` (LIST (YMD 2026 9 7)) (YMD 2026 9 7) BECAUSE "the text has no rule that moves the last day of a period off a day of rest, a holiday or a recess"
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest` `no day of rest` (YMD 2026 9 7) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 7

§ `No rule on deemed service`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a document is treated as served` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "the text has no rule on when a document is treated as served"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a document is treated as served` (YMD 2026 3 14) BECAUSE "the text has no rule on when a document is treated as served"

§ `No definition of a time word`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the number of days the text says is in` `the word day` BECAUSE "the text does not define day, week, month or year"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the number of days the text says is in` `the word week` BECAUSE "the text does not define day, week, month or year"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the number of days the text says is in` `the word month` BECAUSE "the text does not define day, week, month or year"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the number of days the text says is in` `the word year` BECAUSE "the text does not define day, week, month or year"

§ `Art. 1: the day a law begins to bind`

`published on 10 March 2026` MEANS YMD 2026 3 10
`says nothing` MEANS `nothing about when it comes into force`
`a day fixed for itself` MEANS `a day on which it comes into force` OF (YMD 2026 6 1)
`to be fixed later, and fixed as 1 June 2026` MEANS `that the day is to be fixed later` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))
`to be fixed later, and not yet fixed` MEANS `that the day is to be fixed later` OF NOTHING
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`no corrections` MEANS EMPTY

-- the term of art. 1 on its own
#ASSERT `the day the term of art. 1 ends for` `throughout Brazil` `counting from` `published on 10 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 24
#ASSERT `the day the term of art. 1 ends for` `in a foreign State that admits the binding force of Brazilian law` `counting from` `published on 10 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 10
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day the term of art. 1 ends for` `in a foreign State that does not admit the binding force of Brazilian law` `counting from` `published on 10 March 2026` BECAUSE "art. 1 par. 1 starts the binding force of Brazilian law abroad only where it is admitted, and gives no day where it is not"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day the term of art. 1 ends for` `in a foreign State that admits the binding force of Brazilian law` `counting from` (YMD 2025 11 30) BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"

-- the worked case: an Act published on 10 March 2026 that says nothing about when it comes into force
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 24
-- a day later than its publication, and also earlier than 45 days after it
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` (YMD 2026 1 1) `no corrections` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 15
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` (YMD 2025 12 31) `no corrections` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 14

-- the worked case: it comes into force on a day to be fixed later, and the day is fixed as 1 June 2026
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `to be fixed later, and fixed as 1 June 2026` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day an enactment begins to bind` `to be fixed later, and not yet fixed` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` BECAUSE "the enactment leaves its commencement day to be fixed later and no day has been fixed"

-- an enactment that fixes a day for itself displaces the forty-five days
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `a day fixed for itself` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` (`a day on which it comes into force` OF (YMD 2026 3 10)) `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` (`a day on which it comes into force` OF (YMD 2026 3 11)) `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 11
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day an enactment begins to bind` (`a day on which it comes into force` OF (YMD 2026 3 9)) `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` BECAUSE "art. 1 caput lets a contrary provision displace the forty-five days and does not say whether it may fix a day before the official publication"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day an enactment begins to bind` `a day fixed for itself` `in a foreign State that admits the binding force of Brazilian law` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` BECAUSE "art. 1 caput allows a contrary provision and par. 1 does not, so the text does not say whether an enactment's own commencement provision displaces the three months abroad"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day an enactment begins to bind` `a day fixed for itself` `in a foreign State that does not admit the binding force of Brazilian law` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` BECAUSE "art. 1 par. 1 starts the binding force of Brazilian law abroad only where it is admitted, and gives no day where it is not"

-- abroad
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `in a foreign State that admits the binding force of Brazilian law` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 10
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `in a foreign State that admits the binding force of Brazilian law` (YMD 2025 11 30) `no corrections` BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `in a foreign State that does not admit the binding force of Brazilian law` `published on 10 March 2026` `no corrections` BECAUSE "art. 1 par. 1 starts the binding force of Brazilian law abroad only where it is admitted, and gives no day where it is not"

§§ `Art. 1 par. 3 and par. 4: a corrective republication`

-- published 10 March 2026, the law would bind on 24 April 2026
-- a correction before then restarts the forty-five days from the correction
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 3 20)) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 4
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 4 23)) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 7
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 24
-- a correction on the day the law would bind is refused: before it binds (par. 3) or after (par. 4) depends on the moment
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 4 24)) BECAUSE "a corrective republication on the day the law is to begin binding comes before it binds under art. 1 par. 3 or after it binds under art. 1 par. 4, and the text gives no moment of that day"
-- a correction after the law binds is a new law and moves nothing
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 4 25)) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 24
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 9 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 24
-- a correction cannot come before the publication it corrects
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 3 9)) BECAUSE "a corrective republication cannot precede the publication it corrects"
-- two corrections: the second restarts the term again, if it comes before the new day
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 3 20), (YMD 2026 5 3)) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 17
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 5 3), (YMD 2026 3 20)) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 17
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 3 20), (YMD 2026 5 5)) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 4
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 3 20), (YMD 2026 5 4)) BECAUSE "a corrective republication on the day the law is to begin binding comes before it binds under art. 1 par. 3 or after it binds under art. 1 par. 4, and the text gives no moment of that day"
-- abroad, three months from the correction
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `says nothing` `in a foreign State that admits the binding force of Brazilian law` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 8 1
-- a day the enactment fixed for itself is not the art. 1 term, so a correction does not move it
#ASSERT `the day an enactment begins to bind` `a day fixed for itself` `throughout Brazil` `published on 10 March 2026` (LIST (YMD 2026 3 20)) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1

-- par. 4 on its own
#ASSERT `a correction counts as a new law` (YMD 2026 5 1) `when the law binds on` (YMD 2026 4 24)
#ASSERT NOT `a correction counts as a new law` (YMD 2026 4 1) `when the law binds on` (YMD 2026 4 24)
#ASSERT NOT `a correction counts as a new law` (YMD 2026 4 23) `when the law binds on` (YMD 2026 4 24)
#ASSERT `a correction counts as a new law` (YMD 2026 4 25) `when the law binds on` (YMD 2026 4 24)
#ASSERT REFUSED `a correction counts as a new law` (YMD 2026 4 24) `when the law binds on` (YMD 2026 4 24) BECAUSE "a corrective republication on the day the law is to begin binding comes before it binds under art. 1 par. 3 or after it binds under art. 1 par. 4, and the text gives no moment of that day"

§§ `The moment of the day, and what is in force when`

-- the text gives a day and no moment
#ASSERT REFUSED `the second of the commencement day from which a law binds` (YMD 2026 4 24) BECAUSE "art. 1 gives the day on which a law begins to bind and does not say from what moment of that day"

-- the day is known, so the law binds at some moment of it and of every later day, and of no earlier day
#ASSERT NOT `the law binds at some moment of` (YMD 2026 4 23) `when it begins to bind on` (YMD 2026 4 24)
#ASSERT `the law binds at some moment of` (YMD 2026 4 24) `when it begins to bind on` (YMD 2026 4 24)
#ASSERT `the law binds at some moment of` (YMD 2026 4 25) `when it begins to bind on` (YMD 2026 4 24)
-- throughout the day: not before, yes after, and on the day itself the moment decides
#ASSERT NOT `the law binds throughout` (YMD 2026 4 23) `when it begins to bind on` (YMD 2026 4 24)
#ASSERT `the law binds throughout` (YMD 2026 4 25) `when it begins to bind on` (YMD 2026 4 24)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the law binds throughout` (YMD 2026 4 24) `when it begins to bind on` (YMD 2026 4 24) BECAUSE "art. 1 gives the day on which a law begins to bind and does not say from what moment of that day"

§ `Subordinate legislation`

-- the worked case: made on 10 March 2026 and silent about when it comes into force
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day subordinate legislation comes into force` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "art. 1 speaks of a lei and the text has no rule on when subordinate legislation comes into force"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day subordinate legislation comes into force` (YMD 2026 3 11) BECAUSE "art. 1 speaks of a lei and the text has no rule on when subordinate legislation comes into force"
